1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,800
You said Lok Hiu-sin told you
these alphabets stand for

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,960
a high school group called
Youth Investment Organization.

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,680
Why did it become IOY?

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,240
When was the last time you had a
good, hearty laugh?

5
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,960
You get up each day, go to work,
go to school.

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,360
You work your butt off,
doing the same thing.

7
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,280
You try your best against the turmoil
of the world,

8
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,120
then you realized you lost your ability
to laugh.

9
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:23,680
Don't worry!

10
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,760
We'll make you laugh.

11
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,560
The night after tomorrow at 8 o'clock.

12
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,720
Try not to die laughing.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,800
We have a date.

14
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,280
See you in a place you know best.

15
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,920
They want to do another livestream of death?

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,080
(Counting down to the game...)

17
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,680
The last venue for the livestream

18
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,560
is the swimming pool where Ngai Ka-yan died.

19
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,040
They want to re-enact Ngai Ka-yan's death?

20
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,200
What are you looking at?

21
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,800
(Counting down to the game...)

22
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:00,080
This logo is the same as the pin
you found in Ngai Ka-yan's office.

23
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,760
Are they the real killers?

24
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,400
One of them was in Jarvis' office

25
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,080
and broke the vase.

26
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,120
Let's assume Wendy is one of them,

27
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,560
then the whole thing made sense.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,760
Just think, Wendy was lying.

29
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,960
For a few minutes, no one could
confirm her exact location.

30
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,560
Is it possible she broke the vase
at that time?

31
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,920
Or swapped Ngai Ka-yan's cylinder?

32
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,280
But Wendy is Ngai Ka-yan's diehard fan

33
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:27,280
and those IOY kids treat Ngai Ka-yan
as their idol

34
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,000
and created a ranking list for him.

35
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:30,680
Even if they're from the same group,

36
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,440
they have no motive to kill Ngai Ka-yan.

37
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,720
Time to pay the online channel a visit.

38
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,800
These pictures felt like yesterday.

39
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:45,000
Can't believe what happened to this place.

40
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:50,320
Gogo Sir, you didn't come to see me, right?

41
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,440
We came to see Wendy.

42
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,880
She hasn't been here for a long time.

43
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:56,960
Hello?

44
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,640
Gogo Sir, we went to Wendy's flat.

45
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,200
The security guard said she moved out
long time ago.

46
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,040
Thanks.

47
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,560
When was the last time you saw Wendy?

48
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,840
Not since you arrested Auntie Ching.

49
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,840
Did she leave anything behind?

50
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,600
Yes. In the supplies room.

51
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,040
Can we take a look?

52
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,120
How would you describe Wendy's
relationship with Ngai Ka-yan?

53
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,800
Diehard fan with 100% loyalty.

54
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,800
She did everything Jarvis told her to do.

55
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,960
Were they seeing each other?

56
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,000
One of them carrying a torch for the other?

57
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,360
She was Jarvis' diehard fan.

58
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,840
It's normal for her to be crazy about him.

59
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,760
For as long as we've been working together,

60
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:40,120
never saw them making eyes at each other.

61
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,480
J Weekly uploaded...

62
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,880
a video of Helen having an argument with
Ngai Ka-yan in the playground.

63
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,080
According to Auntie Ching,
Wendy uploaded it.

64
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:53,440
Wendy accused Auntie Ching of
murdering Ngai Ka-yan

65
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,480
and threatened to report her.

66
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,200
What's your take on this?

67
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,000
Now that she has disappeared,

68
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,200
maybe she's the thief crying the thief

69
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,160
and tried to frame Auntie Ching for murder.

70
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,920
No way. She's an airhead.

71
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,280
If Wendy contacts you, please let us know.

72
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,280
OK!

73
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,400
Hello? Claim Ngai Ka-yan's body?

74
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:20,640
Wendy...no, Miss Lam is following
up on this.

75
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:26,040
Miss Lam said she needed to contact
Mr. Ngai's mother who's abroad.

76
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,920
That's why we showed discretion
and extended the deadline.

77
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,480
But it has been three months,

78
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,560
now even Miss Lam has disappeared.

79
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:36,360
We'd like the online channel to
wrap this up ASAP.

80
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,160
Excuse me, are you with the FEHD?

81
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:40,480
I'm Ko Man-sum of the Crime Unit,
New Territories East...

82
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,000
Do you recognize her?

83
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:46,240
Yes! I have never met someone like
Miss Lam who takes things to heart.

84
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,600
She did everything herself

85
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,320
and picked the most expensive item.

86
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:53,560
She personally picked out the coffin
from the coffin shop.

87
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,720
When you discussed the details
with Miss Lam,

88
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,240
did you notice anything unusual?

89
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,120
She was polite.

90
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,360
But she lost her temper when
we discussed the burial.

91
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,160
I already applied ahead of time,

92
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,360
what's taking so long?

93
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,440
They said it hasn't been done before.

94
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,760
It may be against regulations.

95
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,440
What does that mean? They won't approve it?

96
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,160
I don't care how much it costs,

97
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,160
I want Jarvis to be buried with the baby.

98
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:19,320
With a baby? Is the baby...

99
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,880
She said it was her baby with Ngai Ka-yan.

100
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,080
The baby just passed away?

101
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:25,840
No. Shortly before Mr. Ngai died.

102
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,080
But the baby is not yet 24 weeks,

103
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,600
the Government will not issue
a Certificate of Cremation.

104
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:34,440
They need to go somewhere else
to cremate the fetus

105
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:36,360
and get a different organization
for the burial.

106
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:40,480
Miss Lam didn't want the baby to be
cremated like a pet,

107
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:44,800
she left it in the hospital and
has been stalling.

108
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,000
The baby cannot be born because of us.

109
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:49,920
I want more than an arbitrary burial.

110
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,000
Hey!

111
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,040
What's this, Uncle?

112
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,200
None of your business. Give it back!

113
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,480
Hey, catch!
Hey...

114
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,120
Don't give it to him...

115
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,640
Hey, give it back!
Don't...

116
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,560
It's a gun!

117
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,320
Nice! Where did you get it?

118
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,680
It looks real.

119
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,400
It is real. Touch it and you're dead,

120
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,760
because I'm an undercover agent.

121
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:36,160
Uncle, you're a UC?

122
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,680
Mr. UC, where did you buy the gun?

123
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,720
Toy shop?

124
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,480
Can't fool you.

125
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,000
I got it from the toy shop over there.

126
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,720
You scraped the gun. Move aside.

127
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,440
You're no fun. Let's go.

128
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,400
Are you sure?

129
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:01,920
If you have money.

130
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,080
Is it a real gun?

131
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,960
We have a deal.

132
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,600
Did you see the look on that guy's face?

133
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,600
He tried to fool us with a toy gun,

134
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:19,720
thinking we were a bunch of kids.

135
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,600
Carl, next time quit while you're ahead.

136
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,480
We have unfinished business.

137
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,520
If we got busted,

138
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,000
we can't play anymore, OK?

139
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,440
OK...it won't happen again.

140
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,440
Jason, who's going in the water?

141
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:40,480
Whoever is the best swimmer.

142
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,120
Nobody?

143
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,600
What a bunch of losers!

144
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,080
Hey, Wendy!

145
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,480
I just decided...for the last video,

146
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,080
I'll go in the water.

147
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,280
How's your leg? Don't try to be brave!

148
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,080
What are you doing?

149
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:09,560
Run...

150
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,640
Can you manage?

151
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,640
Piece of cake.

152
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,640
I have fully recovered.

153
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,120
Nothing must go wrong, OK?

154
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:35,400
Since you let me join the group,

155
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:38,120
I know how important this is to you.

156
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,920
Wendy! Are you Wendy?

157
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,560
I don't know you. I have nothing
to say to you.

158
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:49,680
I'm Jason, a diehard fan of yours
and Jarvis'

159
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,800
Wendy, are you OK?

160
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,520
I saw you upload the video.

161
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,800
Why did you delete it?

162
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:01,240
I ran into a slight mishap.

163
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:05,120
Mishap? Relax, I still have a copy.

164
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,520
I'll send it to you and you can upload it.

165
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,880
Don't. The truth doesn't matter.

166
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,440
Doesn't matter?

167
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,600
Jarvis is dead. Why doesn't it matter?

168
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:16,680
I asked you to come to see if
you want to do something for Jarvis.

169
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,480
What?

170
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,760
J Weekly had a Static Apnea
Challenge before,

171
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,040
they meant to use one of these
to trick one of their own.

172
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:27,240
Wendy, why did you want me to say that?

173
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:29,160
You'll soon find out.

174
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,000
Look over here...

175
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,000
Excuse me...

176
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,240
Leaving already?

177
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,880
Bye, officer!

178
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:35,880
Thanks.

179
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:41,000
I finally know why you want me to say that.

180
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,120
You wanted to lure the cops over
and trick them.

181
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:49,320
Jarvis made a video of a prank on cops.

182
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:52,080
It had high viewership. We must do the same.

183
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,080
You want to make a ranking list?

184
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,120
Smart!

185
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,800
I didn't think of that.

186
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,240
What's next?

187
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,280
Wake up...

188
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:08,800
Get him...

189
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:13,640
In two months, we went from
not knowing how to shoot a video,

190
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,920
to having a bunch of diehard fans.

191
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:17,160
We have come this far,

192
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,320
I won't let this go down the drain.

193
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:22,000
I should thank you for taking the risk

194
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,600
of uploading the video in different places.

195
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:28,320
If IOY didn't have a special meaning for me,

196
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:30,320
I wouldn't rename the channel

197
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,960
and keep its name Agent J Channel.

198
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,400
He's my idol too.

199
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,680
We're kindred spirits.

200
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,240
I should thank you

201
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:40,520
for making videos to carry on
Jarvis' spirit.

202
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,800
Someone inspired me.

203
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,520
But Batman wouldn't want Robin
to go on like this.

204
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,880
What would he want Robin to do?

205
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:52,000
Pull yourself together
and do something meaningful.

206
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,960
For example, finish what he started...

207
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,440
Can I?

208
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,480
I can't believe I did it.

209
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,760
I will achieve Jarvis' target

210
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:06,960
and let him know he'll forever be
our spiritual leader.

211
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:09,960
This will be my last present for him.

212
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:24,280
This will be my last present for him.

213
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,000
But I have a question.

214
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:33,200
You won't tell us the target of
our next prank.

215
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,720
Is there a particular reason?

216
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,960
Clearing out today?

217
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,760
All good things must come to an end.

218
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,280
Anything else you need to ask about Wendy?

219
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:46,600
Before Ngai Ka-yan died,

220
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:49,440
was Wendy injured during filming?

221
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:52,280
Yes. Wendy on the Trampoline.

222
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:56,120
Jarvis made us aim for her sensitive areas.

223
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:58,640
Aim for her shirt, her chest...

224
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,080
Go to Hell!

225
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,920
Keep jumping...keep shooting...

226
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,200
He even threw Mr. Tsui's name in our face,

227
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,840
claiming he really bought the idea.

228
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,400
Hey!
Are you OK?

229
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,120
Are you OK?

230
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,200
Well? Did you get it?

231
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,560
That's exactly what I want!

232
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,920
I like this shot.

233
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,440
Jarvis forced the shoot on us.

234
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:21,320
With no regard for Wendy's feelings.

235
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,840
I didn't expect our target to be an uncle.

236
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,720
This guy appears to be righteous,

237
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,360
but he's very sneaky,

238
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,640
making his pawns do his dirty work.

239
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,200
I have had enough of him.

240
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:37,440
Piece of cake. I'll think of a way
to lure him over.

241
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,880
No sweat! I'll get the job done.

242
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,160
Thank you.

243
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,480
I just looked at the video Tom mentioned.

244
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,720
It was livestreamed on the day
Wendy had a miscarriage.

245
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:57,520
It's highly likely the accident caused
Wendy's miscarriage.

246
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:02,400
She felt Jarvis knew she was pregnant
and still made her do that,

247
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,400
he wanted her to miscarry.

248
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,280
So she wanted to avenge the baby.

249
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:13,080
Happy birthday to you...

250
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:18,200
Gogo Sir, the story came out.

251
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:24,000
The headline reads "24-week baby cannot
be buried with parents"

252
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:27,280
"pray they will be united in Heaven".

253
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:30,080
There were 2,000 shares in half an hour.

254
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,960
The feed should reach Wendy soon.

255
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,560
Good.

256
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,880
My friend agreed to help with the feed

257
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:37,280
and announced the details of
Ngai Ka-yan's funeral.

258
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,400
Along with Cheong's writeup,

259
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,800
Wendy should be moved to tears

260
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:42,520
and show up to see Ngai Ka-yan
for the last time.

261
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:43,680
Let's hope so.

262
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,280
Then we can bring her in for questioning.

263
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,120
There's something I couldn't figure out.

264
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,720
On one hand, she hated Ngai Ka-yan.

265
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,560
On the other hand, she imitates his work

266
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,880
and arranged for his funeral.

267
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:54,480
That's so contradictory,
is she schizophrenic?

268
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,640
Is Wendy really the killer?

269
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,160
Let me show you something.

270
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:00,880
I went over all the videos on J Weekly
these past few days.

271
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,000
There were over a thousand!

272
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:06,520
I found this on the
behind-the-scenes footage.

273
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,880
Happy birthday to...

274
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,600
The IOY pin!

275
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,680
The pin belongs to Wendy.

276
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,440
That can prove she was inside
Ngai Ka-yan's office.

277
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,160
We have reason to believe
she swapped the cylinders.

278
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,160
Was it meticulously planned?

279
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:25,200
Or she killed him accidentally?

280
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,480
(Counting down to the game...)

281
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:29,680
Don't we have 36 hours to go?

282
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,720
Why only 22 hours left? That's tomorrow!

283
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,960
Why did they change the time?

284
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,400
In 22 hours...that should be...

285
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,240
Ngai Ka-yan's vigil.

286
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,000
We must keep a close watch.

287
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:45,080
Please sign here.

288
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,400
Didn't expect you to show up.

289
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:59,360
Anyway...may the deceased rest in peace.

290
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,920
(Counting down to the game...)

291
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:07,000
You're letting those kids do as they please?

292
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,560
They're crazy. They're capable of anything.

293
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,240
There's nothing we can do to stop them.

294
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,480
You guys and Jarvis started this trend.

295
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,760
How could you be so irresponsible?

296
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,440
Let's wait till after the funeral.

297
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,600
After the funeral?

298
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,120
If someone got killed in the prank,

299
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,320
how can you live with yourselves?

300
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:29,400
Miss Lok, can we have a word?

301
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,120
I know what you're worried about.

302
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,840
The funeral is a Police operation.

303
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,080
Don't give them a hard time.

304
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,680
Who's your target?

305
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,200
Wendy?

306
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,280
I knew it.

307
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:51,920
What do you know?

308
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,600
A few months ago when I visited my Mom,

309
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,200
she was preparing a Chinese herb decoction.

310
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,120
She said her colleague Wendy
had a miscarriage.

311
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,800
I didn't give that a second thought.

312
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,000
But since you arrested my Mom,

313
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,400
I've been thinking

314
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:04,440
who else had a motive to kill Jarvis.

315
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,160
I suddenly remember this

316
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,760
and I asked Mom about it.

317
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:11,920
She said Jarvis caused the miscarriage.

318
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,160
If Wendy was the killer,

319
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,280
another Static Apnea Challenge

320
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,240
may not be a simple prank.

321
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,080
You think it's another revenge?

322
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:23,320
Other than Jarvis,

323
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:25,800
did someone else cause Wendy's miscarriage?

324
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,000
He even threw Mr. Tsui's name in our face,

325
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,960
claiming he really bought the idea.

326
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,080
Tsui Chung-tai?

327
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,560
Mr. Tsui!

328
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,440
I didn't expect our target to be an uncle.

329
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,720
This guy appears to be righteous,

330
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,440
but he's very sneaky,

331
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,880
I have had enough of him.

332
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,240
Thanks for coming, Mr. Tsui.

333
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,520
Our livestreaming is about to begin.

334
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,080
The livestreaming started.

335
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,480
Mr. Tsui is at the scene.

336
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:56,160
Wendy is vicious to go after Mr. Tsui.

337
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,680
Help me, officer!

338
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,920
What do you want?

339
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:43,080
I need your help.

340
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,160
With what?

341
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:49,000
The Police found out I was with Jarvis

342
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,040
and he caused my miscarriage.

343
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:54,520
They should suspect me now.

344
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,480
You killed Jarvis?

345
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,520
Jarvis' funeral is tomorrow.

346
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,520
I really wanted to see him.

347
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,840
But I'm sure if I showed up
at the mourning hall,

348
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,120
the cops would arrest me.

349
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:09,000
You knew my Mom is in Lai Chi Kok
detention because of you.

350
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,520
How dare you waltz in here
and tell me this!

351
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,240
What if I turn you in?

352
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:16,600
Go ahead!

353
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,720
They don't have enough to nail me.

354
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:23,280
But on the contrary, Auntie Ching
admitted to swapping the cylinders,

355
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:25,600
she won't get away.

356
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,120
The Police will find a way.

357
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:28,720
Go ahead and call 999.

358
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:31,600
I'm certain after 48 hours,

359
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:35,080
the Police would let me go
because I won't cooperate.

360
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:38,240
But this won't do you or me any good.

361
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,760
You want me to send the cops away?

362
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,720
How could I do that?

363
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:45,080
Make something up.

364
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:48,240
Just say your Mom knew I was with Jarvis.

365
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,760
Tell them I had a miscarriage,

366
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:52,560
or your Mom helped me prepare
the decoction.

367
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:57,840
Convince Gogo Sir I have a second
target to kill.

368
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:01,720
Buy me time so I can see Jarvis.

369
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,000
I don't get it.

370
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:12,720
You said Jarvis caused the miscarriage.

371
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,720
Shouldn't you hate him?

372
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:16,840
Jarvis?

373
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:17,840
Sit down.

374
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,160
Dr. Leung told me you missed
your appointment.

375
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:26,680
Because I wasn't feeling well this morning.

376
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,000
Don't lie to me.

377
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,360
You obviously miscarried.

378
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,320
Why did you pretend you're pregnant?

379
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,840
Because I forced you onto the trampoline

380
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:38,000
and you lost the baby?

381
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,040
You pretended to be pregnant
to get even with me?

382
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:44,240
No, I did not. I was afraid you'd ditch me.

383
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:45,960
That's why I didn't tell you.

384
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:51,200
Silly girl. Who do you take me for?

385
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,560
I promised we'll have the baby

386
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,320
because I respect life.

387
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,840
Now that you tell me the baby is gone,

388
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:02,560
I couldn't wait to celebrate.

389
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:07,520
Wendy, you're still young.

390
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,920
Our channel is taking off,

391
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,880
having a baby now will hold us back.

392
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:14,960
You don't blame me?

393
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,400
Why would I?

394
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,600
Let's put this behind us

395
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,000
and focus on running the channel.

396
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:28,640
You'll always be my best partner, OK?

397
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:34,000
How stupid of you! For this man,

398
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,960
why feel so small and humble?

399
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:39,520
To think a baby can tie down Jarvis?

400
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:41,880
I was too naive.

401
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:44,760
Someone gifted like Jarvis

402
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:48,760
will not slow down for anyone.

403
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:51,520
That's crazy! I can't accept that.

404
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,160
That's why no one deserves to be
with him more than I do.

405
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:56,560
Others would only stop him
from soaring higher.

406
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:58,040
Only I understand.

407
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:01,040
He needs a quiet defender

408
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:03,040
who can help him realize his dream.

409
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,400
If you love him so much,

410
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,360
why did you kill him?

411
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,440
Gogo Sir is back with his team.

412
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,960
He just came inside the funeral home.

413
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:22,320
Wendy, you promised me

414
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,320
after you got your wish,
you'll clear Mom's name.

415
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,760
Come with me and turn yourself in.

416
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:41,920
Did you see Wendy?

417
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:42,960
No.

418
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:55,720
Lok Hiu-sin, what were you thinking?

419
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,680
You chose to help a murderer, of all people?

420
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:00,800
I really had no choice.

421
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:04,240
I don't want Mom to rot in detention.

422
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:06,040
Her health is deteriorating.

423
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,480
She can't take it much longer.

424
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:10,160
Wendy...promised she'll turn herself in.

425
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,280
I had to take a chance.

426
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,160
Turn herself in? Where is she now?

427
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,880
She said she got her wish,
but Jarvis hasn't.

428
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:21,400
Well? You let the last kid go?

429
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,320
Why not? He put on super glue,

430
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:25,600
can't pry open his mouth.

431
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:26,760
He didn't break any laws for pulling a prank

432
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,560
It's pointless to badger him.

433
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:31,720
If Helen didn't interfere,
we would have busted Wendy.

434
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:33,240
Look on the bright side,

435
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:35,600
we couldn't figure out what she was thinking

436
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,480
now at least we know she didn't do it
to avenge the baby.

437
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:42,280
I thought Wendy might have killed
Ngai Ka-yan for the baby,

438
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:44,040
but on second thought...

439
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:46,440
Auntie Ching brought the cylinder of
poison gas to the office.

440
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,480
She couldn't have known about it.

441
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,360
What then?

442
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:52,400
Wendy unknowingly killed Ngai Ka-yan?

443
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,560
Then why did she go inside the office
to swap the cylinders?

444
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:55,680
That's what I want to know.

445
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:58,760
But that's not what worries me...

446
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:02,080
If I killed someone I love by mistake,

447
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,840
I wouldn't know how to go on living.

448
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:05,240
(IOY Channel livestreaming will start soon)

449
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:09,120
(Thanks for everything.)

450
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:11,800
(See you around)

451
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,640
What's this? They're folding the channel?

452
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:15,840
Dream on!

453
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:18,680
IOY Season 2 officially begins.

454
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:22,840
After viewing the first season,

455
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,400
do you want more?

456
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:27,480
Me too. It's OK. We go with the flow.

457
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:30,760
We give you Season 2, right now,
right here...

458
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:35,680
We want to do something different.

459
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,920
All guys? No chicks?

460
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:41,040
Hold your horses.

461
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,680
We save the best for last.

462
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,760
Meet the star of J Weekly,

463
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:51,080
our spiritual leader, Wendy!

464
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:55,120
Long time no see! Did you miss me?

465
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:55,880
Long time no see!

466
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:56,560
I'm showing my face,

467
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:58,160
it means this is not full of crap.

468
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:01,360
We came up with a new game
called Lie Through Your Teeth.

469
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,960
We'll show you a term

470
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,400
and the three of them will take turns
to explain it.

471
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:07,440
Only one of them is telling the truth.

472
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:09,360
The other two are lying

473
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:11,560
but will pretend they're not.

474
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,760
Our viewers can vote

475
00:24:13,840 --> 00:24:16,320
and guess who's telling the truth.

476
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:19,040
If nobody believes the person
telling the truth,

477
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:22,560
then this person will receive
a big punishment!

478
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:25,560
Without further ado, let's roll...

479
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,600
IOY Channel.

480
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,520
Take turns to explain IOY Channel.

481
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:35,040
Don't forget, only one of them
is telling the truth.

482
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:35,840
I'll go first.

483
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:38,680
IOY is short for I opt you.

484
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:40,600
To opt means to choose,

485
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:42,480
IOY stands for I choose you.

486
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:48,000
IOY came from someone I admire...

487
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:52,080
A ring box?

488
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:54,720
Jarvis wants to propose?

489
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:56,680
Wendy, where's the file?

490
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:59,400
Sorry, I saw this and thought it was cute.

491
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:00,560
So I took a look.

492
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:03,880
What's this?

493
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:05,680
I have never seen you wearing it.

494
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:08,080
See the letters on it?

495
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:11,080
Is it YOI?

496
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:14,040
Almost. It's IOY.

497
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,320
The year I started making videos,

498
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:19,760
I was named the most influential
online celebrity.

499
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:22,000
It was given to me as a gift
from the organizer.

500
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:27,520
IOY stands for Influencer of the Year.

501
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:29,840
This pin has great sentimental value.

502
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:32,640
I was afraid of losing it,
so I never wore it.

503
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,440
If you like it...you can have it.

504
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:37,720
But it has great sentimental value.

505
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,040
I'm not giving it to you for nothing.

506
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:40,880
You must try harder.

507
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,760
I have high hopes for you

508
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:45,880
as the next online celebrity.

509
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:47,280
I'll do my best.

510
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:52,520
My goal is to make this channel
the Influencer of the Year

511
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,560
and carry on Jarvis' spirit.

512
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:56,800
That's the meaning of IOY.

513
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,280
Yes...

514
00:26:00,280 --> 00:26:02,600
Wendy made up a brilliant story.

515
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:06,400
But the viewers don't buy it...

516
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:09,360
The IOY bunch should be here.

517
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:10,960
Sir, this is Room 1208.

518
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:20,880
Looks like the viewers don't believe Wendy
is telling the truth.

519
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,000
Then we must...

520
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:26,080
Big punishment...

521
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,040
Open the door!

522
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,400
Big...

523
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:43,000
This is their hideout.

524
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,760
What are these weights for?

525
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:50,360
A clean cut on the rope,

526
00:26:50,760 --> 00:26:52,120
not by natural wear and tear.

527
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:57,320
Climbing rope, weight...

528
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:59,200
they're testing something.

529
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,840
Your punishment is to get us snacks.

530
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:14,840
But from that island...

531
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:19,720
On a zip wire?

532
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:21,120
Of course! You want to walk?

533
00:27:21,360 --> 00:27:22,960
Tens of thousands are waiting for you
to foot the bill.

534
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,960
A bet is a bet, and you lost.

535
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:28,240
These guys are nutcases.

536
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,760
They're livestreaming the zip wire?

537
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,560
Zip wires are not dangerous.

538
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:33,320
But these guys have a prior history.

539
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,880
God knows who's their next prey.

540
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:42,680
I think it's more than a prank.

541
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:46,160
Wait...I recognize this place.

542
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:51,440
Gogo Sir, TCD colleagues couldn't
decipher the livestreaming location.

543
00:27:51,640 --> 00:27:54,120
What about the position?

544
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:56,320
They only know it's Tung Lung Island.

545
00:27:56,560 --> 00:28:00,120
OK, let's split up. We'll try our luck.

546
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:06,000
We have done a rehearsal.

547
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:07,880
Just follow the rehearsal.

548
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:09,920
It's safe. Be careful.

549
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:18,480
Folks, Wendy is ready for her punishment.

550
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:21,280
Give loads of likes to encourage Wendy

551
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:24,240
Hello, Wendy...

552
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:25,200
I'm watching you on live.

553
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,480
Jarvis lied to you.

554
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:30,040
IOY doesn't stand for
Influencer of the Year.

555
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:33,720
It was a high school club called
Youth Investment Organization.

556
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:36,360
Jarvis and I both joined YIO.

557
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,760
That's why he had the pin.

558
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:40,160
Says who? You? Why should I believe you?

559
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:46,320
I don't know what game you're playing.

560
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:48,520
Don't risk your life over Jarvis' lie.

561
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:49,760
It's not worth it.

562
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:53,120
That's why Jarvis is the grandmaster.

563
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:56,360
In a few seconds, he came up with
a story to con me.

564
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:59,240
That's the craft of a master prankster.

565
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:02,440
More reason for me to finish this feat.

566
00:29:02,720 --> 00:29:05,320
You knew he lied to you,
why follow through with it?

567
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:07,080
Whether or not I will succeed,

568
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,760
I must go through with it.

569
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:12,160
If Auntie Ching didn't bring the cylinder
of poison gas to kill Jarvis,

570
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:15,000
I would have tricked him
and earned his recognition.

571
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:17,720
Why? Why did you ruin it?

572
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:21,920
Hello? Wendy...

573
00:29:36,480 --> 00:29:39,320
You again? The zip wire is perfectly legal.

574
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:40,600
Why must you butt in every time?

575
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:42,440
The zip wire is legal.

576
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:44,680
But you purposely sabotaged the rope
to pull a dangerous stunt.

577
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:46,040
That became my business.

578
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:49,520
You won't even bother to show proof
of a trumped-up charge?

579
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:51,320
Showing us a video can charge us
for a crime?

580
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:53,320
How dare you toy with an officer!

581
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:56,520
Gogo Sir, maybe you've been sitting
in your air-con office for too long.

582
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:57,520
You're so out of touch with the world.

583
00:29:57,720 --> 00:29:59,200
This is what the viewers want.

584
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,720
They want something exciting and fun.

585
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,680
The more dangerous, the bigger the draw.

586
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:04,840
You're crazy!

587
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:05,720
Hey!

588
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:07,920
Sir!
Don't get rough...

589
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:24,160
Why did it stop?

590
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:25,840
It's not moving!

591
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:27,240
What happened? Pull her back in!

592
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:30,000
I don't know. During rehearsal,
she was in control. She...

593
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:32,640
Help! Can anyone help me?

594
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:40,680
I can't believe we already have a video
with over 300,000 views.

595
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:43,400
It's much quicker than the target
you set when you started the channel.

596
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:44,720
Not quick enough.

597
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:46,640
Not quick enough?

598
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:50,120
We don't have enough target audience.

599
00:30:51,040 --> 00:30:52,200
When most people hear of prank videos,

600
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:54,920
they assume they're crude and small scale
and not presentable.

601
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:57,120
What do you have in mind?

602
00:30:57,320 --> 00:30:59,080
I want to package it into a show,

603
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:02,280
just like a stage play or concert.

604
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:05,160
Something on a bigger stage,
reaching more people.

605
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,760
I know you can do it.

606
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:12,160
By then...maybe we can take a break.

607
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,240
Stop staring! Save her!

608
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:01,000
What's this?

609
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,000
It'll come in handy.

610
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:06,960
Wendy...yeah!

611
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:16,160
Gogo Sir, not need to overreact!

612
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:18,200
She fooled us all.

613
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:21,760
I watched her try the wristband.

614
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:23,680
It's an inflatable lifebuoy.

615
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:25,680
Everything was for this moment.

616
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:28,760
She staged the accident
during livestreaming.

617
00:32:28,880 --> 00:32:31,080
Oh my God, why didn't I think of that?

618
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:33,600
Brilliant! Conning the viewers was easy,

619
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:35,080
but she fooled us too!

620
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:37,680
When she fell, I was really scared.

621
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:41,480
Wendy, wake up! Quit your act!

622
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:43,240
The livestreaming is finished.

623
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:47,000
She's not breathing! Call 999!

624
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:48,440
What?

625
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:56,400
Mom...

626
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:01,360
Wendy is dead.

627
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:08,560
I'm sorry, Mom! I can't help you.

628
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:15,480
I had ill intentions and wanted to
kill someone.

629
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:22,480
Perhaps...I deserved this punishment.

630
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,840
After Wendy died,

631
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:30,360
I checked her stuff and found this...

632
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:31,680
After several months' preparation,

633
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:33,360
I have finally come to this...

634
00:33:33,840 --> 00:33:36,920
Yuen Kit-ching brought the poison gas
that killed Jarvis,

635
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,840
I was angry at first.

636
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:41,840
But I let it slide.

637
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:43,960
Because Jarvis is dead.

638
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:47,840
The key is how to pass on his spirit

639
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:51,560
so he would approve of me wherever he is.

640
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:54,360
Accidents happen,

641
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:57,680
that's why I decided to record this.

642
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,120
Because I promised Helen,

643
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,600
I would reveal the truth about
Jarvis' death.

644
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:05,960
That day when I mixed up the cylinder of
oxygen with the gas for the starter horn,

645
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:09,400
Tom and Paul rushed over and nervously
tried to stop me.

646
00:34:09,520 --> 00:34:11,360
I found that rather odd.

647
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:17,560
Later Jarvis told me those two ingrates
planned to trick him with a stink bomb.

648
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:20,600
So he decided to trick them with
an oxygen cylinder.

649
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:23,600
On the day of the Challenge,

650
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:25,920
Paul and I had to do another livestreaming.

651
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:28,040
While we were getting ready,

652
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:30,560
I saw Jarvis go inside his office,

653
00:34:30,720 --> 00:34:33,160
and put a blue cylinder in the drawer.

654
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:37,840
Right then, I knew he planned to use it
to trick Tom and Paul.

655
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:41,480
Around that time, Daisy was
hanging around Jarvis,

656
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:44,280
and Jarvis seemed to enjoy it.

657
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,880
He even let her host the Challenge.

658
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:50,000
Remember to CLS. See you next time, bye!

659
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,800
Good! Help me clean this up.

660
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:53,000
I still have a video call.

661
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:57,040
It was 1:50p.m. when Paul and I finished.

662
00:34:57,320 --> 00:34:58,520
You did great!

663
00:34:58,640 --> 00:34:59,440
Thanks.

664
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:00,600
I'll let you take care of this.

665
00:35:01,040 --> 00:35:03,120
I took the garbage to the back stairs,

666
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,840
when I passed by the pantry,

667
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:07,160
I saw Auntie Ching making sweet soup.

668
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:10,080
Paul went inside the conference room
for his video call.

669
00:35:11,760 --> 00:35:15,440
I went back inside but didn't see
Auntie Ching in the pantry.

670
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:17,840
I went back inside the office,

671
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:21,280
and saw Auntie Ching holding a blue cylinder

672
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:24,480
and snuck inside Jarvis office.

673
00:35:25,120 --> 00:35:28,120
I saw her swap the cylinder she was holding

674
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:30,880
with the one Jarvis put inside the drawer.

675
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:33,000
When I look at the cylinder,

676
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:35,760
I thought it was the stink bomb
Tom prepared.

677
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:39,720
My first reaction was Auntie Ching
wanted to trick Jarvis.

678
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:44,800
But soon afterwards, I saw her
switch them back.

679
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:48,440
I thought maybe she was afraid Jarvis
would find out.

680
00:35:49,400 --> 00:35:52,480
Right then, Daisy suddenly came to mind...

681
00:35:52,680 --> 00:35:53,800
Daisy?!

682
00:35:54,080 --> 00:35:55,080
You have time for an interview?

683
00:35:55,200 --> 00:35:56,760
For you? Anytime.

684
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:58,480
Wendy, get us some tea.

685
00:35:58,800 --> 00:35:59,400
Thank you.

686
00:36:02,080 --> 00:36:04,600
If the Challenge was a hit,

687
00:36:04,920 --> 00:36:07,520
Daisy may take my place.

688
00:36:07,760 --> 00:36:11,640
On the contrary, if I finished what
Auntie Ching dared not do,

689
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:14,640
when Jarvis found out I pulled
a prank on him,

690
00:36:14,760 --> 00:36:17,560
he'd be so surprised and impressed.

691
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:20,400
So I went to get the stink bomb
that was left behind.

692
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,360
But I accidentally knocked over the vase.

693
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:25,240
I didn't want anyone to see me,
so I hid myself.

694
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:28,640
Who broke this?

695
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:30,080
I don't know.

696
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:33,000
I was in the supplies room checking
the props of the Challenge.

697
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:34,680
I heard the noise and came to check it out.

698
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:36,240
Did you check on the weight belts?

699
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:37,080
Not yet.

700
00:36:37,240 --> 00:36:39,640
Can you check while I run to the toilet?

701
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:42,320
Auntie Ching, something is broken,

702
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:43,440
can you clean this up?

703
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:45,440
Luckily, nobody saw me.

704
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:48,720
Paul called out to Auntie Ching to
clean up the shards.

705
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:52,800
Since Auntie Ching wasn't holding anything,

706
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:57,040
I figured she left the cylinder
in Jarvis' office.

707
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:03,960
Once I got inside,
I looked for the cylinder.

708
00:37:04,240 --> 00:37:07,000
I didn't expect Auntie Ching
to hide it so well.

709
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:28,640
After I swapped the cylinders,

710
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,840
Auntie Ching and Tom were still cleaning
the shards in the hallway

711
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:33,680
so I stayed there a bit longer.

712
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,160
Don't cut yourself.

713
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:54,240
Soon afterwards, I heard Jarvis came in
with Auntie Ching and Tom.

714
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:56,400
I walked out from the pantry

715
00:37:56,720 --> 00:38:00,120
and Jarvis ordered us to head down
to the pool to set up.

716
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:05,400
You picked the small one
and left the big one for me.

717
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:06,960
You're stronger.

718
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:09,480
As I was heading out, from the corner
of my eye

719
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,880
I saw Jarvis take the cylinder
from the drawer.

720
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,760
I thought I'd hit a home run

721
00:38:14,880 --> 00:38:17,000
and would be able to trick Jarvis.

722
00:38:27,960 --> 00:38:31,280
But he died after he inhaled
from the cylinder.

723
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:35,040
Hey...are you OK?

724
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:36,400
Jarvis...

725
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,480
Are you OK?
Hey...

726
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:39,040
Don't scare me...
Wake up...

727
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:40,120
My mind went completely blank.

728
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:43,320
I thought Daisy took the cylinder
prepared by Tom and Paul.

729
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:45,320
Tom never got along with Jarvis,

730
00:38:45,440 --> 00:38:48,200
did Daisy work with him to kill Jarvis?

731
00:38:51,840 --> 00:38:53,320
Later, I found out it wasn't Daisy.

732
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:55,240
Then why did Auntie Ching do it?

733
00:38:55,480 --> 00:38:56,880
Where did she get the poison gas?

734
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,840
Did she take it from Tom?

735
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,280
Is Tom the killer?

736
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:02,440
Auntie Ching already quit.

737
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:03,560
Why?

738
00:39:04,040 --> 00:39:05,840
Why did Auntie Ching quit?

739
00:39:06,080 --> 00:39:07,760
Is she really scared?

740
00:39:11,120 --> 00:39:13,200
Wendy! Are you Wendy?

741
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:15,200
Jason later sent me a video.

742
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:17,840
It was Jarvis who paralyzed Helen.

743
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:21,160
How is Helen related to the online channel?

744
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,400
Mom, how nice of you to pick me up
from work?

745
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:25,080
So I followed Helen

746
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:27,640
and found out Auntie Ching is Helen's Mom.

747
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:30,720
The gas came from Auntie Ching.

748
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:33,000
She wanted to kill Jarvis
but couldn't do it.

749
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:35,560
I wanted Jarvis recognition

750
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,800
and killed him by mistake.

751
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:39,760
No!

752
00:39:40,040 --> 00:39:42,320
Auntie Ching deleted the video

753
00:39:42,720 --> 00:39:44,800
but I had no intention to inform the Police.

754
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:49,080
I don't want the cops to stop me
from carrying on Jarvis' legacy.

755
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:54,000
I know I will succeed. Jarvis will see it.

756
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,160
Where did this come from?

757
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:58,720
The GoPro when she was on the zip wire?

758
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:24,160
Wendy considered Ngai Ka-yan her idol.

759
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:28,320
Like him, she died in front of the camera.

760
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:34,800
Helen just finished giving her statement.

761
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:37,880
From Lam Sum-ling's phone,
we found a self-made video

762
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:41,720
that can prove Auntie Ching removed
the poison gas.

763
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:45,120
Legally, that won't constitute as murder.

764
00:40:45,600 --> 00:40:48,280
But she stole a hazardous gas,

765
00:40:48,600 --> 00:40:51,320
she's guilty of possession of a dangerous
substance and theft.

766
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:52,840
She cannot post bail yet.

767
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:05,880
Ngai Ka-yan, I never understood why
you enjoy being a prankster.

768
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:08,520
Because you were deprived of love?

769
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:11,520
You want other people's attention?

770
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:16,680
Mom, I want to play in the park.

771
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:18,240
Ten minutes.

772
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:19,320
What?

773
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:22,200
Ngai Ka-yan, when I bought you
the watercolor,

774
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,880
what did you promise me?

775
00:41:24,040 --> 00:41:26,280
Play less and study more.

776
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:29,000
I'll pick you up in 20 minutes.

777
00:41:29,080 --> 00:41:30,120
Yeah...

778
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:48,000
Who did this?
Why?

779
00:41:48,160 --> 00:41:49,600
Who did this?

780
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:52,000
Superman against monsters...

781
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:59,400
Ngai Ka-yan, it's wrong to trick other kids.

782
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:00,640
I understand.

783
00:42:00,880 --> 00:42:02,640
I bought you a sketch book.

784
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:05,040
You can take it out and share with
other kids.

785
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:06,240
Why must you do this?

786
00:42:06,520 --> 00:42:07,280
I know.

787
00:42:07,560 --> 00:42:08,360
Let's go.

788
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:11,120
Mom, there's a mosquito on your back.

789
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:12,040
Let me swat it for you.

790
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:13,760
OK, it's dead.

791
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:16,000
Good boy. Thank you.

792
00:42:18,640 --> 00:42:21,640
I remember that time at the
high school playground,

793
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:24,840
I told you your prank paralyzed me.

794
